/* book exam traps: Heading, track and bearing are three different things. A radial of 030 says where the aircraft is relative to the station; the nose may point anywhere. | Outbound on the 030 radial you track 030°; inbound on the same radial you track 210°. Forgetting the 180° flip costs marks. | In σ ÷ sin θ, σ is the error across each line, not along it. Along the line the measurement gives no information at all. | A small cocked hat does not prove a good fix. If all three lines share one bias, such as a common timing error, they make a tiny triangle around a wrong point. */
