/* book Worked example 2: Q: An aircraft at 9 km altitude reads a DME slant range of 150 km. What is its ground distance from the transponder?
   1. d = √(r² − h²) = √(150² − 9²).
   2. 150² = 22500 and 9² = 81, so d = √22419.
   3. d = 149.7 km.
   Answer: The ground distance is 149.7 km. */
